{"content":[{"c":["SEPHARVAIM, SEPHARVITES*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of five cities and its inhabitants who were transported to Samaria after the fall of Israel to Sargon II, king of Assyria, in 722 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.17.24","r":"2Kgs.17.24","rawR":"2Kgs.17.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.17.24","value":"2Kgs.17.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 17:24"},"). The Sepharvites were remembered for their abominable practice of offering their children as burnt sacrifices to their gods Adrammelech and Anammelech. In a taunting message to King Hezekiah of Judah (715–686 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), King Sennacherib of Assyria (705–681 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") warned that as the gods and kings of Sepharvaim were not able to prevent her fall to the Assyrians, so too it would be with Jerusalem and Hezekiah’s God (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.34","r":"2Kgs.18.34","rawR":"2Kgs.18.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.34","value":"2Kgs.18.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.36.19","r":"Isa.36.19","rawR":"Isa.36.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.36.19","value":"Isa.36.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 36:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.37.13","r":"Isa.37.13","rawR":"Isa.37.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.37.13","value":"Isa.37.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"37:13"},"). The location of Sepharvaim is uncertain. It is probably identifiable with the Syrian city of Sibraim near Damascus (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.47.16","r":"Ezek.47.16","rawR":"Ezek.47.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.47.16","value":"Ezek.47.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 47:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"SepharvaimSepharvites","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 17:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.17.24","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.17.24","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.17.24"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 18:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.34","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.18.34","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.18.34"},{"anchorText":"Is 36:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.36.19","rawQueryValue":"Isa.36.19","sourceRefExact":"Isa.36.19"},{"anchorText":"37:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.37.13","rawQueryValue":"Isa.37.13","sourceRefExact":"Isa.37.13"},{"anchorText":"Ez 47:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.47.16","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.47.16","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.47.16"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"52b98a2d106a3a82e8195b96b1380f90716dc33227bbd78a8a84241af0495db0","sourceItemName":"SepharvaimSepharvites","sourceItemOrder":154,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"SepharvaimSepharvites","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Sepharvaim, Sepharvites*","title":"Sepharvaim, Sepharvites*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}